WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.620
SPEAKER: Our program helps
students learn, build,

00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:06.740
and get certified on
Google Cloud Platform.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.930
The Associate Cloud
engineer track

00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:10.595
consists of the
following benefits.

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:19.240
First, students and faculty
receive a 100% discount

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:22.630
to pursue the architecting
with Google Cloud Platform

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:26.470
specialization on Coursera.

00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:29.770
In addition, we are also
making hands-on training

00:00:29.770 --> 00:00:34.600
available in the form of
self-based labs on Qwiklabs.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.570
Here, again, there's
a 100% discount

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:42.420
to access the Cloud Architecture
Quest and other labs.

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:46.200
Finally, we want both
students and faculty

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.820
to prepare for certification.

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:52.210
To prepare for and earn the
Associate Cloud Engineer

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:56.890
Certification, faculty who have
completed the specialization

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:02.040
receive a 100% discount
on the certification exam.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.120
A student discount
is also available.

00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:08.360
Students who are familiar
with basic concepts related

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:12.380
to operating systems,
networking, databases,

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:17.450
and programming are good
candidates for this program.

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:20.840
What do you and your students
learn in the Associate Cloud

00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:23.430
Engineer Track?

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:26.760
The Architecting with Google
Cloud Platform Specialization

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.530
on Coursera comprises
six courses.

00:01:30.530 --> 00:01:32.960
The specialization
introduces learners

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.960
to the comprehensive and
flexible infrastructure

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:40.850
and platform services provided
by Google Cloud Platform.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.370
Through a combination
of presentations,

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:47.840
demos, and hands on labs,
learners explore and deploy

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:52.100
solution elements, including
infrastructure components

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:57.590
such as networks, systems,
and application services.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:01.860
This course also covers
deploying practical solutions,

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:05.430
including securely
interconnecting networks,

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:09.419
customer supplied encryption
keys, security and access

00:02:09.419 --> 00:02:14.420
management, coders and billing,
and resource monitoring.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:17.970
In the cloud architecture
quests spanning 11 hours

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:20.760
the labs have been
curated to give learners

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:23.640
hands on practice with
topics and services

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.180
that appear in the Associate
Cloud Engineer Certification

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.380
exam.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:32.850
From IAM, to networking, to
Kubernetes engine deployment,

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:36.540
this quest is composed of
specific labs that will put

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:39.180
your GCP knowledge to the test.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.670
In addition to this
quest, learners also

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:45.650
have access to other labs.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.630
The Associate Cloud
Engineer track

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:50.510
must be completed in 16 weeks.

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:54.420
This slide shows a
suggested timeline.

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.270
Complete the Architecting
with Google Cloud Platform

00:02:57.270 --> 00:03:00.960
Specialization within
the first nine weeks.

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:03.330
Complete the Cloud
Architecture Quest

00:03:03.330 --> 00:03:07.400
and additional hands-on
labs by week 16.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:11.420
Complete the Associate Cloud
Engineer Certification exam

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:14.620
before the voucher
expiration date.

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:20.040
Students can definitely
race ahead of the timeline.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.110
Learners completing
the Architecting

00:03:22.110 --> 00:03:25.020
with Google Cloud
Platform Specialization

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:28.590
will earn a Coursera
completion certificate,

00:03:28.590 --> 00:03:31.320
which can be shared with
prospective employers

00:03:31.320 --> 00:03:34.080
and a professional network.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:38.090
The Associate Cloud Engineer
Certification exam objectively

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:42.740
measures an individual's ability
to demonstrate the critical job

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:45.320
skills required for the role.

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:48.140
The exam duration is two hours.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:52.130
The format is multiple
choice and multiple select.

00:03:52.130 --> 00:03:54.740
This exam must be
taken in person

00:03:54.740 --> 00:03:58.110
at one of our testing
center locations.

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:01.800
For more details, visit the
Associate Cloud Engineer

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:05.390
Certification web page.

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.520
Some of the faculty
responsibilities

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:12.220
are registering for and
attending online onboarding

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.370
sessions, enrolling
and managing students

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:17.380
on your Coursera program--

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:22.390
ideally your cohort has 60
to 200 students per faculty,

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:25.810
monitoring student's learning
progress and nudging students

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.340
who may be falling behind.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:32.690
conducting study jams to support
student's learning progress--

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:35.930
study jams are essentially
workshops that you conduct

00:04:35.930 --> 00:04:40.020
with your students, earning
your Associate Cloud Engineer

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:42.540
Certification, and
encouraging students

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:47.040
to become certified to
validate technical expertise.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.970
For more information,
refer to the faculty FAQs.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:56.750
Google Cloud has ensured
that you, as faculty,

00:04:56.750 --> 00:05:00.140
are enabled to run this
program successfully

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:03.030
in your college or institution.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.880
You get administrative
access on Coursera

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:09.920
to monitor students learning
progress in real time.

00:05:09.920 --> 00:05:13.220
The Faculty Resource Center
provides enhanced support

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:16.740
to faculty with program
related materials,

00:05:16.740 --> 00:05:21.960
including student FAQs and a
guide on conducting study jams.

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.850
Your students will
also get access

00:05:23.850 --> 00:05:27.080
to a student Resource Center.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:31.070
Faculty and students can contact
the Coursera and Qwiklabs

00:05:31.070 --> 00:05:35.380
support teams for any
platform related issues.

